# Local dev working folder — see dev-docs/README.md for the canonical layout.
# Durable: `plans/` (actionable plans/backlog), `designs/` (design-decision
# reference), `bench/scripts/` + `bench/results/`, `todos.md`. Auto-purged by
# the dev-docs-cleanup skill: `temp/` (>1d, offload large output here to dodge
# the token gate), `bench/out/` (>14d, built graphs / raw dataset dumps),
# `bin/` (>7d, soft-deleted). Local working state, never committed — with ONE
# exception: `bench/scripts/` IS tracked. Harnesses there are hand-authored
# source that would otherwise exist in exactly one copy, in a tier nothing ever
# purges — a stray `rm -rf` loses work no backup, review or CI ever saw. The
# directory is empty today; un-ignoring it now means the first harness written
# here is tracked by default instead of silently unbacked. Build output and
# captures produced inside a harness dir stay ignored.
# (`/dir/*` + `!/dir/sub/` so a subdir can be re-included.)
/dev-docs/*
!/dev-docs/bench/
/dev-docs/bench/*
!/dev-docs/bench/scripts/
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/target/
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/__pycache__/
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/node_modules/
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/*.kgl
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/*.kgle

# Inbox of feedback/coordination notes (`unread/` = needs action, `read/` =
# archive). Kept at the repo root; local working state, never committed —
# see the "Inbox hygiene" section in CLAUDE.md and inbox/README.md.
/inbox/

# Claude Code local settings (skills / working config; local state, never
# committed — mirrors kglite's .gitignore).
/.claude/

# Python virtualenvs / caches
/.venv/
/.venv*/
/venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
/.pytest_cache/
/.ruff_cache/
/.mypy_cache/
/.hypothesis/

# Rust build artifacts
/target

# Built distribution artifacts — wheels + sdists are produced fresh by the
# release workflow (maturin-action → PyPI), never committed.
/dist/
/wheels/

# Compiled extension modules (built by maturin develop)
*.so
*.pyd

# Built / downloaded dataset artifacts — regenerable from the loaders, never
# committed. Heavy raw fetches + built graphs are disposable (dev-docs/bench/out).
*.kgl
# …except small, byte-deterministic test fixtures built from a seeded input.
!tests/fixtures/*.kgl
/data/

# Internal feature-goalpost / competitive-survey planning doc — local working
# state, kept out of the public repo and the shipped wheel. Belongs in
# dev-docs/ per house convention; excluded here so going-public doesn't leak
# competitive positioning. Maintainer: move to dev-docs/plans/ if you want it
# tracked privately.
/
# Coverage
.coverage
coverage.xml

# Sphinx docs build output
docs/_build/

# macOS
.DS_Store
